CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> The Rigveda, the earliest corpus of Indian literature, contains about 1,028 hymns and was passed on orally for centuries. Vedic society was organised in tribes, and an important tribal body was the sabha, the smaller assembly of select elites, along with the larger samiti. The Vedic idea of rita means cosmic order. "
   "(i) How many hymns does the Rigveda contain? (ii) Name the smaller assembly of select elites. (iii) What does 'rita' mean? (iv) Explain how the assemblies acted as a check on the king.",
   "(i) About 1,028 hymns (1). (ii) Sabha (1). (iii) Cosmic order (1). (iv) The sabha and samiti discussed matters and supported or opposed policies, so a king who ignored them could lose support (2).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Kautilya's Arthashastra describes the seven limbs of the state and says that a state is like a wheel that works only when all parts work together. Under the Mauryas the basic land tax was about one-sixth of the produce. Emperor Ashoka followed a policy of Dhamma. In a Gupta district office, a banker, a caravan trader and an artisan sat with officials. "
   "(i) Who wrote the Arthashastra? (ii) What was the basic land tax under the Mauryas? (iii) What was Ashoka's policy called? (iv) What does the Gupta district office show about local administration?",
   "(i) Kautilya (1). (ii) About one-sixth of the produce (1). (iii) Dhamma (1). (iv) That economic groups such as bankers, traders and artisans took part in running local administration (2).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A Chola village chooses its leaders by writing names on palm-leaf tickets and putting them in a pot; a child draws the tickets. The village assembly looks after irrigation, revenue and disputes. The Cholas built the Grand Anicut for water supply. A Nashik cave inscription records deposits made with weavers' guilds. "
   "(i) Name the method of selection used in the Chola villages. (ii) What does the Grand Anicut show about the Cholas? (iii) Which animal was the Chola emblem? (iv) Why can guilds be compared to banks, and what did the village assembly do?",
   "(i) Kudavolai (lot) (1). (ii) Their skill in irrigation engineering (1). (iii) Tiger (1). (iv) Guilds accepted deposits and gave loans like banks (1); the assembly handled irrigation, revenue collection and disputes (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

